id: ops-release-1020-recovery
title: Recover the historical 2026.10.20 GitHub Release with verified release evidence
description: "Recover the missing v2026.10.20 GitHub Release without changing its tag or npm artifact. The release commit omitted its changelog section because the historical pm-changelog scripts excluded empty release windows; current main was repaired separately. Verify registry identity, signed provenance, source ancestry, tag identity, full tarball/tree equality and committed package identity before recovering notes from a later committed changelog. Add an independent missing/duplicate section gate before publication. Local repair preflight must reach the guarded release write; actual GitHub Release creation remains delegated to the daily job's existing --repair after review and merge. Keep this item open for orchestrator verification."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T10:54:35.891Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T17:01:06.629Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T03:11:34.131Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit on main 1ceb53b69d4bb0eea323625744fe9200a38bb267: merged PR #205 (36478d717b40a5f73a49b06b486c1c83f93d39bc, merged 2026-10-25T11:22:43Z). REST GET releases/tags/v2026.10.20 returns HTTP 404. Inspected release-repair.ts and .github/workflows/release.yml; the changelog fix does not create a historical GitHub Release. Owner decision and separately authorized historical release recovery remain required. Leave open; no release or tag is changed. Existing behavioural revert evidence is retained; this tracker-only audit changes no runtime functions."
  "2026-10-27T02:55:57.395Z",codex-agent,"Reconfirmed for the release-changelog recurrence: git show v2026.10.20:CHANGELOG.md lacks the matching section, while v2026.10.26 and current main contain it exactly once. The repair error refers to immutable historical notes, not current main. This remains a separately authorized release-recovery task; ops-release-changelog-stability fixes pending-to-tag generation drift."
  "2026-10-27T03:02:46.663Z",codex-agent,"The exact release workflow audit command was re-run behind a GitHub GET-only guard: npm run verify:release-completeness -- --repair. It reported github_release_absent: v2026.10.20 and FAIL - release repair refused: committed changelog must have exactly one section for 2026.10.20, with exactly one failure. All source/provenance/tarball checks before historical-note extraction succeeded. No release or tag was created. A passing live audit still requires separately authorized historical recovery; changing current generator output cannot alter the immutable tagged file."
  "2026-10-27T10:05:07.734Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit of PR #216 (eac1589d0fd598ae0c5375b4d83806418b86c5e4): the current-main changelog fix does not recover the missing historical v2026.10.20 GitHub Release. Its immutable release commit lacks matching notes, so automatic repair refuses. This owner-decision item stays open; release creation or historical evidence changes require a separate decision and authorization."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:02.894Z",glm-agent,"Root cause diagnosis (worktree at origin/main 089e803): the v2026.10.20 tag, npm 2026.10.20 dist.gitHead and the remote tag all name release commit ee029738 ('Release pm-ops v2026.10.20', authored by github-actions[bot]). That release commit bumped package.json, package-lock.json, manifest.json, index.ts and dist/index.js but did NOT touch CHANGELOG.md: git show v2026.10.20:CHANGELOG.md ends at the 2026.10.15 section - zero sections for 2026.10.20 (and none for 10.16-10.19). git log v2026.10.15..v2026.10.20 -- CHANGELOG.md is empty, so the 2026-10-20 run created its release commit during the changelog generation-drift window (the pending-to-tag drift fixed separately in ops-release-changelog-stability / PR #205, which restored main's changelog afterwards). Current main is healthy: the committed changelog has exactly one section for every one of the 61 release-tag versions, and npm view pm-ops@2026.10.20 dist.gitHead returns the same ee029738. The blocker is therefore NOT current main's changelog but the repair's single note source: repairReleaseCompleteness extracts notes only via git show <release-commit>:CHANGELOG.md, and that immutable commit can never gain a section, so every daily run's --repair refuses forever. Fix plan: keep the release commit's own changelog as the primary note source, and fall back to the audit-time committed changelog (regenerated by changelog:full --all-release-tags and enforced by changelog:check plus a new pre-release section gate) only when the historical commit lacks exactly one section; never read uncommitted working-tree state."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:04.612Z",glm-agent,"Revert proof (behavioural revert run in a disposable copy of the package worktree, never the checkout): with releaseNotesFor reverted to the pre-fix single-source read of the release commit's changelog, the two new repair tests fail ('a drift-window release commit without its own section recovers notes from the audit-time committed changelog' and 'a release missing its section in both committed changelogs still refuses before writes'); with the section gate's audit gutted and unwired from release:check, the gate tests fail ('the drift shape fails before a release starts', 'verify audits a checkout's changelog against injected tags' and 'the release gate chain runs the section check before a release starts'). All focused tests pass on the fixed implementation (release-repair.test.ts: 27/27; verify-release-changelog-sections.test.ts: 7/7)."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:06.357Z",glm-agent,"Local dry-run of the repair (the script has no dry-run flag, so the GitHub Release write boundary was stubbed; everything before the write ran for real from a scratch script, with npm reads on a clean config): the report-only audit shows exactly one failure ('release tag v2026.10.20 has no corresponding GitHub Release'); the repair run verified npm evidence for pm-ops@2026.10.20 (attested provenance, registry identity and gitHead match the tag commit), verified the published tarball against the release tag tree, verified the committed package identity, and then planned the release notes for v2026.10.20 as 'No tracked changes.' - the exact section from the audit-time committed changelog. The only remaining step was the GitHub Release write, which the daily release job's own --repair will perform on its next run; no tag, npm artifact or GitHub Release was changed here."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:08.161Z",glm-agent,"Resuming the existing recovery branch and evidence. The requested branch/worktree already exists with three commits and no open PR. Fresh fetch includes v2026.10.28; will bring the branch up to current main without rewriting tracker history, regenerate via the pinned changelog scripts, repeat the local guarded repair and behavioural revert proof, then run npm/Bun release gates with at most two workers. Release creation remains delegated to the daily job under the queue rule forbidding manual releases."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:30.265Z",glm-agent,"Updated to origin/main 983b632 (v2026.10.28). Restored the item and history from main and re-recorded this branch's intended comments, files and linked tests with the pinned CLI, preserving main as an exact history prefix. Earlier branch audit records remain in prior commits."
  "2026-10-28T15:43:27.280Z",glm-agent,"Fresh diagnosis confirms the concrete generator policy defect: at v2026.10.20, package.json used pm-changelog 2026.10.16 without --include-empty in changelog, changelog:full or changelog:check. Empty release windows were omitted, so regeneration and equality checking agreed on a file missing 2026.10.16 through 2026.10.20. git log -p v2026.10.15..v2026.10.20 -- CHANGELOG.md has no commits; ee0297384c5854dc4e372a6bf96ac2ceca6fdf7a changed five version files only. Commit 36478d7 (PR #205) later added the missing sections using --include-empty and No tracked changes. npm view pm-ops@2026.10.20 dist gitHead confirms gitHead ee0297384c5854dc4e372a6bf96ac2ceca6fdf7a and tarball integrity sha512-8Xz98Bff2d0prXzexNyiAwFLDZ2LanaK+S2uFFgzXwClTuSwrq42O5I36NTUn/MVtWQtBSEiaWXUzQPqsfp/rQ==. The repair still read only the immutable old changelog. Regenerated current CHANGELOG.md through changelog:full, then changelog:check passed with no diff from current main."
  "2026-10-28T15:45:09.378Z",glm-agent,The automatic merge driver emitted a clone-local union/reanchor receipt before the required main-prefix restoration. Reconciliation refused that superseded receipt without validated staged evidence and wrote no history. Preserved it outside the active tracker; no reanchor was accepted. Byte comparison confirms main history remains an exact prefix. Local health also reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for the host-discovered pm-github extension; the pinned CLI itself is installed correctly and dependency pins are unchanged by this fix.
  "2026-10-28T15:48:58.570Z",glm-agent,"Fresh local execution: npm run verify:release-completeness -- --repair has no built-in dry-run flag. Ran that exact CLI behind an external GitHub GET-only guard: all registry, signature/provenance, tag/source ancestry, full npm tarball/tree and committed package identity checks ran unchanged. It reached only the expected v2026.10.20 release creation with notes exactly No tracked changes. The guard refused the write, so the CLI intentionally ended with one guard failure rather than the former missing-section refusal. No release/tag/npm write occurred. The daily job must create the historical release with its existing --repair on its next authorized run. Focused repair and section-gate suites pass 34/34, zero failures/skips; the section audit passes all 62 currently released versions. Full npm release gate is running with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config."
  "2026-10-28T15:57:09.015Z",glm-agent,"First isolated npm release gate: 1491 tests passed, 0 failed, 2 pre-existing optional real-data tests skipped (configured fleet repositories are not supplied). Typecheck, lint, duplication and docstrings passed. Coverage correctly refused the new error-formatting ternaries: release-repair.ts 99.34% branches and the section verifier 93.33%, while all statements/functions/lines were 100%. Simplifying both diagnostics through String(error) removes redundant type-specific formatting without weakening the parser or coverage thresholds; re-running focused checks, revert proof and the full gates."
  "2026-10-28T15:59:14.181Z",glm-agent,"Pinned pm test ops-release-1020-recovery --run --progress --timeout 1200 passed all 3 linked commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-repair.test.ts (27/27), node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/verify-release-changelog-sections.test.ts (7/7), and npm run verify:release-changelog-sections (62 release versions). Zero focused failures/skips. Automatic test-result recording is disabled by project policy, so this comment preserves the results without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-28T16:00:11.229Z",glm-agent,"Fresh behavioural revert proof in a disposable clone of b99f06c: reverted only releaseNotesFor to the historical single-source implementation and rebuilt; the 2 selected recovery regressions both failed. Restored it, then replaced only auditChangelogSections with the former no-check behaviour; 3 of 7 section-gate tests failed, including the missing/duplicated/empty drift fixture and checkout audit. Restored both fixed functions in finally, rebuilt and reran the 9 selected regressions: 9 passed, 0 failed/skipped. The package worktree was never mutated for these reverts."
  "2026-10-28T16:30:09.504Z",glm-agent,"The final isolated npm gate reached 100% statements/branches/functions/lines for both changed runtime modules (release-repair.ts and scripts/verify-release-changelog-sections.ts), but failed on the unchanged regular-input child-startup timeout already tracked by ops-input-startup-timeout. It reported 1490 passed, 1 failed, 2 optional configured-repository skips; the timed-out child also left unrelated assurance.ts/index.ts refusal branches uncovered. Recorded the observation on that existing follow-up rather than creating a duplicate. No startup deadlines, coverage thresholds or unrelated product code were changed."
  "2026-10-28T16:32:48.564Z",glm-agent,"The existing reader-startup timeout also reproduces outside coverage on Node 24.19.0 and Node 26.12.0 (5/6 reader tests pass on each). Kept the recovery fix scoped and recorded evidence on ops-input-startup-timeout. Publishing the reviewable branch with this local gate blocker disclosed, then running bun run release:check with Node 26 and checking PR CI; no release/tag/npm artifact writes are authorized here."
  "2026-10-28T16:35:15.361Z",glm-agent,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/224 at head 53a83a12ed259a731b4dcb0ff0713fb21aeb51c5. The PR discloses the existing local reader-startup gate blocker and deferred historical release write. Both changed history files are verified byte-prefix extensions of origin/main. The required bun run release:check is running under nvm Node 26.12.0 with isolated Git/npm configuration; PR CI is also running. Will update evidence and release this claim before handoff, without closing either item."
  "2026-10-28T16:51:13.744Z",glm-agent,"Validation complete for the recovery implementation at 53a83a12ed259a731b4dcb0ff0713fb21aeb51c5: local bun run release:check passed 1491 tests, 0 failed, 2 configured-fleet opt-in skips and 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 41 measured sources. PR CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40727229905 passed Node 22 and Node 26 npm AND Bun release gates (each 1491 passed, 0 failed, 2 opt-in skips), both Windows consumer jobs, tracked-project health and packed compatibility consumers; CodeQL also passed. The local npm reader-startup failure and isolated controls remain recorded on ops-input-startup-timeout. Greptile returned a trial-expired notice, while neutral/skipped review checks are not approvals. No runtime changes follow this tested implementation; remaining writes are tracker evidence and claim release. After that bookkeeping push, latest-head CI must be checked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/224/checks before closure. Historical v2026.10.20 creation remains delegated to the release job's --repair; the local guarded repair verified source, provenance and complete tarball equality before the write boundary."
  "2026-10-28T17:01:06.629Z",glm-agent,"CI handoff within the queue's existing wait limit: bookkeeping head f0cc3ec72c874b2bfee01c9225660576e633769e has pending Node 22, Node 26 and Windows Node 22 jobs in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40730289992, plus queued CodeQL in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40730290461. Windows Node 26 passed. The earlier source-identical implementation head 53a83a1 passed both npm and Bun gates on Node 22/26, both Windows jobs and CodeQL; local Bun also passed 1491 tests with all four coverage dimensions at 100% across 41 sources. This final handoff record changes tracker data only, so its push needs fresh latest-head checks at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/224/checks; pending/neutral/skipped checks and unavailable Greptile are not approval. Claim is already released, both items remain unclosed, and the orchestrator owns final-head verification and closure. The historical release write remains deferred to the release job's --repair."
